    "en": [
      "Terminal Station at Night, Macon, Ga, Ellen Payne Odom Genealogy Library Postcard Collection, Moultrie-Colquitt County Library System"
    ]
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Postcard (color, linen textured, white border, divided back, 3 1/2 x 5 1/2 inches) titled Terminal Station at Night. Macon, Georgia. – 14. The 200 – foot long building, built of sandstone in the Beaux Arts style, was completed in 1916 to serve as the principle railroad hub for central Georgia. At the height of its activity, the station had 15 lines emanating from it and saw some 100 passenger trains a day during the 1920s and -30s. The station closed in 1975. It was purchased by the City of Macon in 2002. No descriptive text on reverse. Postage required – 1 cent stamp."
    ]
  },
